  "acceptance_requirements": [
    "Financial source, original token, durable terminal owner and main-DB accounting must commit together; lost ACK requires authoritative replay, not assumed rollback.",
    "Held/reserved subscription requests retain original user, amount and period; source receipt and token changes must roll back together.",
    "Task/Midjourney terminal transitions, net source shares, original credential identity, missing metadata quarantine and recovery fairness require their actual current matrix leaves.",
    "Realtime observed segments reserve the original request; aggregate actual usage is charged once, including modality and cache-presence facts.",
    "Historical rows with unproved delivery/identity are read-only review data, not authority to compensate balances.",
    "Dedicated empty native databases, actual dialect selection and strict required-descendant checker remain mandatory.",
    "Full normal/race/vet/build, nested-module DTO tests/build, and actual frontend build/browser verification are separate required evidence, not inferred from focused test or compile-only embed fixtures."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Separate LOG_DB uses a single application emission attempt after a newly applied financial commit, not cross-database atomic delivery. External display may be missing or duplicated; reconcile its stable key against the authoritative main-DB receipt.",
    "SQLite immediate/deferred behavior is recorded separately; only native multi-connection tests establish row-lock concurrency.",
    "Owned subprocess assertions count actual child leaves once, never add parent proxies to totals.",
    "Old failure logs, invalid fixture results and compiler errors remain unaltered and separately classified."
  ],
